From 61ac9f98384bfef9920c44875cb1ec1864fe14eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SN Fast Sync <snfast@localhost.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:36:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(snjs): a custom sync server also gets its websocket on
 the same host (wss://HOST/ws)

The sign-in screen's custom server setting calls setCustomHost(host) without a websocket URL, which cleared the websocket URL: a
self-hosted server with push never got its websocket unless the app was built with the URL preset. Now the websocket URL defaults
to the same host under /ws (wss for https, ws for http) and keeps the path of the server URL in front of /ws (a server that is
reached under a secret path, https://HOST/p/KEY, gets wss://HOST/p/KEY/ws); nothing is guessed for localhost. With patch 0014 this
makes the runtime "custom sync server" setting enough to get push from our own server. Applied to every target except the stock
comparison app (patches/customserver has its own folder, so changing it never starts the iPhone build by itself).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
